From: Andrei Lepikhov <andrei.lepikhov@pgedge.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Demo planner probe: raise a flag when a parameterized nestloop is built

Debugging-only core patch for contrib/pg_probe_explain, an alternative to
0001-planner-probe-JOIN_SEMI.patch - both export the same boolean, so apply one
or the other, not both.

It raises planner_probe_hit in create_nestloop_path() whenever the inner path
draws its parameters from the outer relation, i.e. whenever a parameterized
nestloop path is built.  The flag goes up regardless of what the cost comparison
later decides, so a query is logged even when the final plan contains no
nestloop at all - which is exactly the case EXPLAIN cannot show you.

Note what is *not* being tested here.  A nestloop path can also be
parameterized from above, meaning the join as a whole needs parameters from some
outer relation; that condition is `required_outer` being non-empty, and swapping
the test is a one-line change if that is the question you want to ask.

Applies to REL_18_STABLE and, with offsets, to 1C_18_1.
---
--- a/src/backend/optimizer/util/pathnode.c
+++ b/src/backend/optimizer/util/pathnode.c
@@ -43,6 +43,12 @@
 } PathCostComparison;
 
 /*
+ * Probe flag reported to loadable modules.  Here it is raised whenever the
+ * planner builds a parameterized nestloop path; see the comment in pathnode.h.
+ */
+bool		planner_probe_hit = false;
+
+/*
  * STD_FUZZ_FACTOR is the normal fuzz factor for compare_path_costs_fuzzily.
  * XXX is it worth making this user-controllable?  It provides a tradeoff
  * between planner runtime and the accuracy of path cost comparisons.
@@ -2693,6 +2699,17 @@
 		outerrelids = outer_path->parent->relids;
 
 	/*
+	 * Report to interested modules that a parameterized nestloop was built:
+	 * the inner path draws its parameters from the outer relation, so the
+	 * executor can drive the inner side one outer row at a time.  Whether the
+	 * path then wins on cost is a different question, and deliberately not
+	 * asked here - catching the paths that were built and lost is the whole
+	 * point of the probe.
+	 */
+	if (bms_overlap(inner_req_outer, outerrelids))
+		planner_probe_hit = true;
+
+	/*
 	 * If the inner path is parameterized by the outer, we must drop any
 	 * restrict_clauses that are due to be moved into the inner path.  We have
 	 * to do this now, rather than postpone the work till createplan time,
--- a/src/include/optimizer/pathnode.h
+++ b/src/include/optimizer/pathnode.h
@@ -17,6 +17,15 @@
 #include "nodes/bitmapset.h"
 #include "nodes/pathnodes.h"
 
+/*
+ * Debugging aid: a probe flag that the planner sets when a condition of
+ * interest is met while building paths, so that a loadable module can notice
+ * it once planning is over.  The core only ever sets the flag; clearing it
+ * before planning is the reader's responsibility.  See
+ * contrib/pg_probe_explain.
+ */
+extern PGDLLIMPORT bool planner_probe_hit;
+
 
 /*
  * prototypes for pathnode.c
